//@ bundled
// tests/samples/stdlib/somelib.fin is the specification and it says "Empty lib".
//
// This one is a directory rather than a file, and that is the whole point of it.
// `extern_as.fin:9` is emphatic about why: "IMPORTANT: THIS IS SO IMPORTANT BECAUSE WE
// DO NOT GIVE ANY PATH TO IT SO HOW DOES THE COMPILER KNOW WHERE TO IMPORT THIS
// LIBRARY, as we assume somelib is a directory containing modules." So `import
// "somelib";` has to resolve a *directory* off a search path, and the resolution it
// exercises is ModuleLoader.cpp's third candidate: `<base>/<name>/index.fin`. A file
// named somelib.fin would resolve through the first candidate and leave the directory
// form untested.
namespace std {
}
